The fix for crbug 576742430 (restricted: "Handle DOM mutations during text
replace in editing commands"): chromium/src main commit
fa67974bfd1ac902f428fd279915ad485016b2a0 (main@{#1745213}), merged to the 159
branch as e2f0f843af (8154@{#853}) and to 157's. Its 158 merge (Gerrit 8832377)
is pending, as of 8127@{#1889}.

Synchronous event listeners can run while an editing command (e.g. a page's
execCommand('insertText'/'insertHTML')) replaces text in a node, and mutate or
disconnect the text node and the selection endpoints the command still uses: a
memory-safety bug in the renderer, reachable from a page. The fix copies the
replacement string before mutating the DOM, clamps the updated offsets, and
aborts the command if the selection endpoints became invalid.

This is the main commit's change without its tests (insert_text_command_test.cc,
replace_selection_command_test.cc), regenerated against 158's files (the same at
the .37 tag and at #1889; the main commit's hunks apply to them at offsets only,
with no fuzz). The result is byte-identical to the files of the pending 158
merge's current patchset. Drop this once 158 gets the fix (check that the merged
change is the same).

